sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick, 2026-11-07): the release of a task VM as its own run, for a task start that failed or a group that ended without a cancel run. The same steps end a cancel (docs/cli/tasks/cancel.mmd). The identity stays.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · the end of a task start that failed
  %% kind: task_vm.slot_release
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>the identity is releasing
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-release
  SW->>H: Delete the VM<br/>and its seed clone
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus delete --force` and the seed clone; a rerun finds them gone
  %%> - beside it, the claim's model key is revoked at the model router; the Pi token goes with the VM
  %%> - no Node, DNS, Metrics or hub peer change
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>identity free
    Note over GW: Free the identity<br/>forget the claim's keys
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the identity is `failed`; while it holds a model key the slot rule releases it again, then it enrols it again
  end
